{"clip_id": "Eng_007066", "text_verbatim": "and now, words and their stories from V.O.A. Learning English.", "annotation_status": "L1_DONE", "transcript_source": "manual"}
{"clip_id": "Eng_007067", "text_verbatim": "Springtime is a time of renewal and growth.", "annotation_status": "L1_DONE", "transcript_source": "manual"}
{"clip_id": "Eng_007068", "text_verbatim": "Many plants end their long winter sleep.", "annotation_status": "L1_DONE", "transcript_source": "manual"}
{"clip_id": "Eng_007069", "text_verbatim": "and form new buds and shoots.", "annotation_status": "L1_DONE", "transcript_source": "manual"}
{"clip_id": "Eng_007070", "text_verbatim": "Beautiful flowers will soon be showing their bright colors.", "annotation_status": "L1_DONE", "transcript_source": "manual"}
{"clip_id": "Eng_007071", "text_verbatim": "and the grass will grow thicker and greener again.", "annotation_status": "L1_DONE", "transcript_source": "manual"}
{"clip_id": "Eng_007072", "text_verbatim": "Some flowers bloom in a very noticeable way.", "annotation_status": "L1_DONE", "transcript_source": "manual"}
{"clip_id": "Eng_007073", "text_verbatim": "But that is not the case with grass.", "annotation_status": "L1_DONE", "transcript_source": "manual"}
{"clip_id": "Eng_007074", "text_verbatim": "Imagine you were sitting in a grassy field.", "annotation_status": "L1_DONE", "transcript_source": "manual"}
{"clip_id": "Eng_007075", "text_verbatim": "and you have only one job.", "annotation_status": "L1_DONE", "transcript_source": "manual"}
{"clip_id": "Eng_007076", "text_verbatim": "to watch the grass grow.", "annotation_status": "L1_DONE", "transcript_source": "manual"}
{"clip_id": "Eng_007077", "text_verbatim": "That does not sound very interesting.", "annotation_status": "L1_DONE", "transcript_source": "manual"}
{"clip_id": "Eng_007078", "text_verbatim": "In fact, it sounds really boring.", "annotation_status": "L1_DONE", "transcript_source": "manual"}
{"clip_id": "Eng_007079", "text_verbatim": "That idea is what gives us the expression like watching grass grow.", "annotation_status": "L1_DONE", "transcript_source": "manual"}
{"clip_id": "Eng_007080", "text_verbatim": "We use this expression to describe an experience that is uninteresting.", "annotation_status": "L1_DONE", "transcript_source": "manual"}
{"clip_id": "Eng_007081", "text_verbatim": "Another good word to describe it is tedious.", "annotation_status": "L1_DONE", "transcript_source": "manual"}
{"clip_id": "Eng_007082", "text_verbatim": "We use this expression in many situations.", "annotation_status": "L1_DONE", "transcript_source": "manual"}
{"clip_id": "Eng_007083", "text_verbatim": "Let's hear a few examples.", "annotation_status": "L1_DONE", "transcript_source": "manual"}
{"clip_id": "Eng_007084", "text_verbatim": "After the politician won his campaign?", "annotation_status": "L1_DONE", "transcript_source": "manual"}
{"clip_id": "Eng_007085", "text_verbatim": "He gave a two-hour long acceptance speech.", "annotation_status": "L1_DONE", "transcript_source": "manual"}
{"clip_id": "Eng_007086", "text_verbatim": "two hours", "annotation_status": "L1_DONE", "transcript_source": "manual"}
{"clip_id": "Eng_007087", "text_verbatim": "It was as much fun as watching grass grow.", "annotation_status": "L1_DONE", "transcript_source": "manual"}
{"clip_id": "Eng_007088", "text_verbatim": "I really don't like watching long sports games.", "annotation_status": "L1_DONE", "transcript_source": "manual"}
{"clip_id": "Eng_007089", "text_verbatim": "It's like watching grass grow.", "annotation_status": "L1_DONE", "transcript_source": "manual"}
{"clip_id": "Eng_007090", "text_verbatim": "Now, grass grows on the ground all the time.", "annotation_status": "L1_DONE", "transcript_source": "manual"}
{"clip_id": "Eng_007091", "text_verbatim": "And usually we don't give it much thought.", "annotation_status": "L1_DONE", "transcript_source": "manual"}
{"clip_id": "Eng_007092", "text_verbatim": "If you stand in one place for a long time,", "annotation_status": "L1_DONE", "transcript_source": "manual"}
{"clip_id": "Eng_007093", "text_verbatim": "The grass will continue to grow under your feet.", "annotation_status": "L1_DONE", "transcript_source": "manual"}
{"clip_id": "Eng_007094", "text_verbatim": "for people who are always active, always moving, always on the go.", "annotation_status": "L1_DONE", "transcript_source": "manual"}
{"clip_id": "Eng_007095", "text_verbatim": "We can say they don't let grass grow under their feet.", "annotation_status": "L1_DONE", "transcript_source": "manual"}
{"clip_id": "Eng_007096", "text_verbatim": "We can also say, beneath their feet.", "annotation_status": "L1_DONE", "transcript_source": "manual"}
{"clip_id": "Eng_007097", "text_verbatim": "and sometimes we use this expression as a command.", "annotation_status": "L1_DONE", "transcript_source": "manual"}
{"clip_id": "Eng_007098", "text_verbatim": "Don't let the grass grow beneath your feet.", "annotation_status": "L1_DONE", "transcript_source": "manual"}
{"clip_id": "Eng_007099", "text_verbatim": "Get back to work!", "annotation_status": "L1_DONE", "transcript_source": "manual"}
{"clip_id": "Eng_007100", "text_verbatim": "She certainly doesn't let the grass grow under her feet.", "annotation_status": "L1_DONE", "transcript_source": "manual"}
{"clip_id": "Eng_007101", "text_verbatim": "She's been traveling non-stop for over a year.", "annotation_status": "L1_DONE", "transcript_source": "manual"}
{"clip_id": "Eng_007102", "text_verbatim": "And that's all the time we have for this words in their stories.", "annotation_status": "L1_DONE", "transcript_source": "manual"}
